-- title:
--   Base change commutes with the degeneracy map q↦ q^ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N$ and $\ell$ be natural numbers with $\ell \neq 0$. Write $\mathbb{Q}$-level field $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the set of series $q\mapsto$ `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d$ of $N$, and `laurentBaseChange L F₀` for the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$ under the ring homomorphism `coeffEmb L`, which pushes a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ forward along $\mathbb{Q}\to L$. Let $x \in L((q))$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ lying in $F_N$. Then `coeffEmb L x` lies in `laurentBaseChange L F_N`, and the value at this element of the $L$-algebra map `heckeBetaBar L N ℓ` from `laurentBaseChange L F_N` to `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull (N * ℓ))`, which is induced by the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ on $L((q))$ (the `embDomain` ring homomorphism along multiplication by $\ell$ on the exponent group $\mathbb{Z}$), equals, as an element of $L((q))$, the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb L` of the series `qExpand ℚ ℓ x` obtained by the same substitution performed over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the degeneracy embedding $\beta\colon f(\tau)\mapsto f(\ell\tau)$ between modular function fields of levels $N$ and $N\ell$ with extension of the coefficient field: on $q$-expansions $\beta$ is the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$, and it is defined over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the study of the places and the Galois/Frobenius behaviour of the base-changed modular function fields, where elements of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational field must be moved through $\beta$ and through the coefficient embedding in either order.
